Keep a saved cursor for each screen, leave autowrap out of it, and add DECLRMM

DECSC and SCOSC saved one cursor for both screens, so that saving on the
alternate screen lost the main screen's. Keep one for each, as xterm does,
and save and restore the one of the screen in use.

DECRC and SCORC restored autowrap, which xterm's do not: xterm saves the
cursor's position, attributes, character sets and origin mode, and leaves
DECAWM as it is.

Add DECLRMM, CSI ? 69 h and l, as a flag only: while it is set, CSI s is
xterm's DECSLRM and not SCOSC. There are no left and right margins, so
DECSLRM does nothing, and DECRQM still reports the mode as not recognized.

